This fragment of the source should be helpful:

if (your_race(&mons[pm])) {
	    if (!CANNIBAL_ALLOWED()) {
		if (Upolyd)
			You("have a bad feeling deep inside.");
		You("cannibal!  You will regret this!");
		HAggravate_monster |= FROMOUTSIDE;
		change_luck(-rn1(4,2));		/* -5..-2 */
	    } else {
		You("feel evil and fiendish!");
		u.ualign.record++;
	    }
	}

As an orc, all monsters represented by "o" (goblins included) are
considered to be the same race as you. So eating a goblin counts as
cannibalism, which would give you intrinsic aggravate monster, which
is a Bad Thing--except that as an orc, you're exempt from penalties
for cannibalism, and instead get +1 to alignment (the CANNIBAL_ALLOWED
flag above).

